  "scope_statement": "This is a manifest-level scenario card. If the scenario file contains a Country value, that value is the scenario authoring default; the run certificate records the countries actually materialised and executed.",
  "summary": "Acute treatment of COPD exacerbations with inhaled bronchodilators and oral steroids.\nThis scenario exposes the parameters for the Inhaled Salbutamol, Ipratropium Inhaler, and Oral Prednisolone interventions.\nThis was the mapping for the CR2 Scenario in Appendix 3 simulations.\nInhaled Salbutamol reduces the disability weight of persons living with COPD by 14.8%, providing bronchodilation for symptom relief.\nIpratropium Inhaler continues at baseline coverage.\nOral Prednisolone reduces the disability weight by 33.7% for severe COPD exacerbations, targeting 12% of the COPD population who experience acute worsening.\nOral Prednisolone remains at baseline coverage for the first projection year and then increases to ninety-five percent coverage for the rest of the projection.\nThis should typically be run as a comparison scenario, with the baseline scenario being the COPD Baseline, or modified versions with different target coverage levels for acute treatment protocols.\n",
  "title": "Appendix 3 - CR2 Scenario"
}
